{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000dac5","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0af07-89f4-7ab1-8e06-e8d6537acf87"},"sequence":3005,"recorded_at":1780531400006005,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"5cf12a39-f5bf-4b30-87e7-6389df903783","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"5cf12a39-f5bf-4b30-87e7-6389df903783","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"5cf12a39-f5bf-4b30-87e7-6389df903783"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0af27-01a1-74b2-8673-aba79435c4d5"},"task_id":"01a0af27-01a1-74b2-8673-aba79435c4d5","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0af27-01a1-74b2-8673-aba79435c4d5","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev2/results-rev2.md`.\n1|# TASK-260830-2atgj4 results rev2: republish on fresh trunk (refresh/reconcile record)\n2|\n3|Role: developer. Run: republish-rev1 (rebase onto trunk, no\n4|re-implementation). Worktree:\n5|`.temp/STORY-260830-1oqfec/worktree` on\n6|`task-board/story/STORY-260830-1oqfec`, candidate left UNCOMMITTED\n7|for the handoff snapshot. Status at handoff: ready for review.\n8|\n9|The rev1 implementation record\n10|(`TASK-260830-2atgj4_results.md`: 11 property tests, RED-first\n11|`resolveWinner` fix, 8 narrowing mutants killed, traceability\n12|story-close) stands unchanged: this run changed no product code\n13|beyond the mechanical base reconciliation below, and re-ran the\n14|full validation suite plus the property and mutation batteries on\n15|the fresh base. All green.\n16|\n17|## Refresh record (exact commands and OIDs)\n18|\n19|Old Story base: trunk `62d4463`; checkpoints `0ebb7fa` (2f5393)\n20|and `1b8e75a` (3g12yp). Fresh trunk authority:\n21|`e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311` (STORY-260917-158jyi:\n22|release-agnostic cataloggen `-adopted` check).\n23|\n24|1. `git fetch origin`\n25|2. `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2atgj4` ->\n26|   stops at the 2f5393 replay with `UU LOGBOOK.md` in the\n27|   retained replay worktree\n28|   `.temp/base-refresh/replay-2355938507/worktree`\n29|   (`REBASE_HEAD=0ebb7faf656ebc9059d7f51f652fee08c680f8bf`;\n30|   HEAD side = trunk's 3lt2xv block, theirs = the 2f5393 block,\n31|   both under `## 2026-09-17`, exactly as predicted).\n32|3. Built the resolved LOGBOOK (markers removed, both blocks kept,\n33|   trunk 3lt2xv first then 2f5393, one blank line between,\n34|   everything else byte-identical;\n35|   sha256 `6524d022b343605e2a860556350b7e0bcf028754bfdf5062c2d880ba8ef1f17b`,\n36|   432317 bytes) and wrote the retained\n37|   `resolution-template.json` shape with one resolution bound to\n38|   checkpoint `0ebb7faf656ebc9059d7f51f652fee08c680f8bf`.\n39|4. `task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2atgj4\n40|   --replay-resolutions /tmp/resolutions-2atgj4.json` -> 2f5393\n41|   replay accepted; stops at the 3g12yp replay with\n42|   `UU LOGBOOK.md` in\n43|   `.temp/base-refresh/replay-3296328019/worktree`\n44|   (`REBASE_HEAD=1b8e75ac703eaa5b6a3f9bb009709d74a759c015`).\n45|5. Added the second resolution bound to\n46|   `1b8e75ac703eaa5b6a3f9bb009709d74a759c015` (content keeps\n47|   3lt2xv, then the 3g12yp block, then 2f5393;\n48|   sha256 `bd7944f0aa6f0b52eeaddedb9b5643c9123103450cb817629ea14c39fa046b83`,\n49|   434919 bytes) and reran -> `refresh_advanced`,\n50|   `BranchOID=ef71cef5e094d085a3dde8bdc805709f27a85c4a`.\n51|\n52|## Replayed-checkpoint verification\n53|\n54|- Chain: `ef71cef` (replayed 3g12yp) ->\n55|  `67445fa2da460b7c6610e78294b72627538c00cf` (replayed 2f5393)\n56|  -> `e4e3e88` (trunk). `git verify-commit` good on both\n57|  replayed commits (oparin@me.com).\n58|- Whole-tree `git diff <original> <replayed> --stat` shows only\n59|  the trunk delta (3lt2xv board files, LOGBOOK +6, README,\n60|  `internal/catalog/*`, `task-board.config.json`); none of the\n61|  checkpoints' own files (sessrepo, fencing, traceability,\n62|  sessquery) differ. Each replayed checkpoint's own file set is\n63|  intact except the LOGBOOK resolution.\n64|\n65|## Candidate reconciliation (by hand, no wholesale checkout)\n66|\n67|`git checkout HEAD -- task-board.config.json\n68|internal/catalog/catalog.go internal/catalog/catalog_test.go\n69|internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main.go\n70|internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen/main_test.go .task-board`\n71|restored every trunk-changed path outside the 13 candidate paths\n72|(`task-board.config.json` now equals HEAD, zero diff).\n73|\n74|- LOGBOOK.md: inserted trunk's 3lt2xv block verbatim between the\n75|  candidate 2atgj4 block and the 3g12yp block. Order is now\n76|  2atgj4, 3lt2xv, 3g12yp, 2f5393 (newest-first by wall time);\n77|  `git diff` vs HEAD is purely additive (48 insertions, 0\n78|  deletions).\n79|- README.md: restored trunk's `-adopted` regenerate block and\n80|  Go-toolchain row cell verbatim; kept the candidate\n81|  property-suite section, the `ownership properties` harness\n82|  table row, and the 110->113 count. Diff vs HEAD: 64\n83|  insertions, 1 deletion (the count line only).\n84|\n85|`git status` shows exactly the 13 candidate paths (9 modified +\n86|`internal/fencing/ownership_properties_test.go`,\n87|`internal/sessrepo/lease_properties_test.go`,\n88|`internal/sessstate/ownership_properties_test.go`,\n89|`internal/sessstate/testdata/mutate_properties.py`); no\n90|`__pycache__`, no `.pyc`.\n91|\n92|## Re-run validation on the fresh base (all local, real exits)\n93|\n94|Full 26-command suite from `task-board.config.json` (command 21\n95|is the `-adopted` form), all exit 0:\n96|\n97|| # | Command | Result |\n98|| --- | --- | --- |\n99|| 1 | gofmt clean | OK (empty) |\n100|| 2 | `go build ./...` | exit 0 |\n101|| 3 | `go vet ./...` | exit 0 |\n102|| 4 | `go test ./... -count=1 -v` | exit 0; 27 ok, 0 FAIL; 19910 `--- PASS` |\n103|| 5 | `go test ./... -race -count=1` | exit 0; 27 ok, 0 FAIL |\n104|| 6 | `go test ./... -cover -count=1` | exit 0; 27 ok (sessstate 92.4%, sessrepo 86.6%, fencing 97.5%) |\n105|| 7-11 | scalar + canonicaljson fuzz | 5/5 pass |\n106|| 12-19 | secconftest fuzz | 8/8 pass |\n107|| 20 | tracecheck | exit 0 (`acceptance_cases=113`, `clauses_discharged=28/485`) |\n108|| 21 | cataloggen `-adopted -check` | exit 0 |\n109|| 22-23 | linux/windows cross builds | exit 0 |\n110|| 24 | JSON validation | exit 0 |\n111|| 25 | `task-board validate` | exit 0 (191 pre-existing board notices) |\n112|| 26 | `git diff --check` | exit 0 |\n113|\n114|Property suites on the fresh base:\n115|\n116|- Focused `go test ./internal/sessstate ./internal/sessrepo\n117|  ./internal/fencing -run '^TestOwnership' -count=1`: exit 0,\n118|  all 11 properties pass\n119|  (`props-focused.log`).\n120|- Mutation battery `mutate_properties.py`: harness exit 0; all\n121|  8 `N-` plants KILLED by their named properties\n122|  (`N-compare-tiebreak` and `N-union-detail-first` by\n123|  `TestOwnershipUnionOrderIndependent`, both loser-drop plants\n124|  by `TestOwnershipLoserHistoryPreserved`, `N-create-clock` by\n125|  `TestOwnershipStoreClockNonAuthority`, `N-expiry-absolute` by\n126|  `TestOwnershipGateClockNonAuthority`, both gate plants by\n127|  `TestOwnershipGateSingleAuthorizedOwner`);\n128|  `C-harmless-comment` SURVIVED (applied),\n129|  `C-not-applied` NOT_APPLIED, `C-compile-failure`\n130|  COMPILE_OR_HARNESS_FAILURE; both controls exit 0\n131|  (`mutants-run.log`, `mutants/mutants-full.json` + per-plant\n132|  raw logs).\n133|\n134|The indented `--- FAIL` lines inside the verbose suite log are\n135|the expected inner-harness plant failures captured by passing\n136|tests; top-level `^FAIL` count is 0 in every batch.\n137|\n138|## Evidence attached (rev2)\n139|\n140|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_results-rev2.md` (this file)\n141|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_conformance-matrix-rev2.md`\n142|- `TASK-260830-2atgj4_producer-evidence-rev2.tar.gz` (real\n143|  gzip: 26-command logs, focused property log, mutation\n144|  battery logs + `mutants-full.json` + per-plant raw logs)","final_result":true}}}
